### Lab 5 — URL-based access restrictions (SecurityConfig)
### Users (seeded by DataInitializer): user/user123 (USER), admin/admin123 (ADMIN), superadmin/superadmin123 (SUPERADMIN)
### Run the login requests first: they store tokens and the CSRF cookie value.

### Login as USER
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "user", "password": "user123" }

> {%
    client.global.set("userToken", response.body);
    const setCookie = String(response.headers.valueOf("Set-Cookie") || "");
    const m = setCookie.match(/XSRF-TOKEN=([^;]+)/);
    if (m) client.global.set("csrf", decodeURIComponent(m[1]));
%}

### Login as ADMIN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "admin123" }

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body); %}

### Login as SUPERADMIN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "superadmin", "password": "superadmin123" }

> {% client.global.set("superadminToken", response.body); %}

### 1. Anonymous -> public route (expected 200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/access/public

### 2. Anonymous -> user route (expected 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/access/user

### 3. USER -> user route (expected 200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/access/user
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 4. USER -> admin route (expected 403)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/access/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 5. ADMIN -> admin route (expected 200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/access/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6. ADMIN -> superadmin route (expected 403)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/access/superadmin
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 7. SUPERADMIN -> superadmin route (expected 200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/access/superadmin
Authorization: Bearer {{superadminToken}}

### 8. USER -> create item (expected 403)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "user item", "description": "should be rejected", "price": 10 }

### 9. ADMIN -> create item (expected 200)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "admin item", "description": "created by admin", "price": 99.99 }

> {% client.global.set("itemId", response.body.id); %}

### 10. ADMIN -> delete item (expected 403, SUPERADMIN only)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}

### 11. SUPERADMIN -> delete item (expected 200)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{superadminToken}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrf}}
